WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:05.180
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:10.670
These amazing images were all made by an AI
called DALL-E 2.

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:17.160
This AI is endowed with a diffusion-based
model, which means that when we ask it something,

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:24.199
it starts out from noise, and over time, it
iteratively refines this image to match our

00:00:24.199 --> 00:00:25.600
description better.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:33.030
And, over time, magically, an absolutely incredible
image emerges.

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:39.160
This is a neural network that was given a
ton of images, and a piece of text that says

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:41.850
what is in this image.

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:44.110
That is one image-caption pair.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:48.920
DALL-E 2 is given millions and millions of
these pairs.

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:52.440
So, what can it do with all this knowledge?

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:57.990
The key takeaway here is that it does no,
or very little copying from this training

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:03.000
data, but it truly comes up with novel images.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.000
How?

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:11.330
Well, after it had seen a bunch of images
of koalas, and separately, a bunch of images

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:18.350
of motorcycles, it starts to understand the
concept of both, and it will be able to combine

00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:22.440
the two together into a completely new image.

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:28.860
Previously, we also compared these works to
what real human artists are capable of.

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:35.090
And, in my opinion, this tool should not be
framed at all as Team Humanity versus Team

00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:36.090
AI.

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:42.130
I believe this should be framed as Team Humanity,
supercharged by Team AI.

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:45.110
Here’s an example of that.

00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:52.229
And the results are so good, and it is so
easy to use, I said, on several occasions

00:01:52.229 --> 00:01:56.549
that this is going to change the world of
art creation as we know it.

00:01:56.549 --> 00:02:05.130
And, you are an experienced Fellow Scholar,
so you may ask the question, okay, but how?

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:10.899
Here are 5 beautiful examples of how artists
are already using it.

00:02:10.899 --> 00:02:12.920
One, texture synthesis.

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:14.519
Oh yes.

00:02:14.519 --> 00:02:20.540
Whenever we see these beautiful animation
movies or video games, we see a lot of real-looking

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:22.370
content in there.

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:27.620
The roads are realistic, the buildings and
hills are also realistic.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:33.309
We can get a great deal of help in making
them realistic by…taking photographs of

00:02:33.309 --> 00:02:37.739
real objects and importing them into our virtual
world.

00:02:37.739 --> 00:02:40.750
But there is a problem.

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:41.750
What is the problem?

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:43.329
Well, let’s see together.

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:44.999
Let’s take a photo.

00:02:44.999 --> 00:02:49.019
There is a stain on the wall, is that the
problem?

00:02:49.019 --> 00:02:52.799
No, that’s not the problem, we can cut that
out.

00:02:52.799 --> 00:02:59.199
Now, we need to extend this texture, but since
this is just a small snippet, and we have

00:02:59.199 --> 00:03:03.860
long walls and big buildings to fill in a
video game.

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:06.309
So, what do we do?

00:03:06.309 --> 00:03:08.189
We start tiling it.

00:03:08.189 --> 00:03:09.890
And, uh-oh.

00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:11.839
Now that is the problem.

00:03:11.839 --> 00:03:18.349
It is quite visible what happened to this
texture, it has been extended, but at the

00:03:18.349 --> 00:03:23.639
cost of seams and discontinuities appearing
in the image.

00:03:23.639 --> 00:03:27.280
So, how do we get a seamless texture from
this?

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:34.499
Well, DALL-E 2 hopefully understands that
this is a rock wall, and, can it fix this?

00:03:34.499 --> 00:03:38.930
Now, hold on to your papers, and let’s see
together.

00:03:38.930 --> 00:03:40.260
Yes it can!

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:41.260
Amazing!

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:47.979
Now let’s have a look at it attached to
a real virtual object and see how it looks

00:03:47.979 --> 00:03:49.040
in practice.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:50.639
Oh my.

00:03:50.639 --> 00:03:51.779
This is gorgeous.

00:03:51.779 --> 00:03:53.620
I love it.

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:59.579
Here is an even more difficult example with
paint peeling off the wall.

00:03:59.579 --> 00:04:02.119
This is the real-world phone photo.

00:04:02.119 --> 00:04:05.029
And the tiled version with the seams.

00:04:05.029 --> 00:04:07.129
And now, DALL-E 2.

00:04:07.129 --> 00:04:08.209
Wow!

00:04:08.209 --> 00:04:12.290
I could never tell that this image is not
a real photo.

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:16.060
And, have a look at it added to a video game.

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:17.209
So good.

00:04:17.209 --> 00:04:23.110
By the way, these are Stan Brown’s works,
who used DALL-E 2 to great effect here.

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:28.460
Make sure to check out his work, for instance,
he also made these amazing materials for one

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:32.790
of my favorite games of all time, Path Of
Exile.

00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:37.389
The link to his work is available in the video
description.

00:04:37.389 --> 00:04:45.069
Just imagine using the free 3D modeling tool,
Blender and this plugin to create roads, and

00:04:45.069 --> 00:04:51.449
you can make it an asphalt road, dirt road,
or make it look like pavement in just a couple

00:04:51.449 --> 00:04:53.509
clicks with DALL-E 2.

00:04:53.509 --> 00:05:00.770
Two, DALL-E 2 is now able to generate real
human faces too, and sometimes they come out

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:02.360
really well.

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:05.009
And sometimes, not so much.

00:05:05.009 --> 00:05:10.970
No matter, in these cases, we can use a face
restoration program to fix some of the bigger

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:18.389
flaws and run it through a super-resolution
program to add more details, and bam.

00:05:18.389 --> 00:05:19.580
There we go.

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:20.580
Fantastic.

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:27.219
And, if we have a portrait that works for
us, we can plug it into an amazing tool called

00:05:27.219 --> 00:05:32.569
Deep Nostalgia to create a virtual animated
version of this person.

00:05:32.569 --> 00:05:34.729
How cool is that.

00:05:34.729 --> 00:05:36.469
What a time to be alive!

00:05:36.469 --> 00:05:39.469
Three, this one speaks for itself.

00:05:39.469 --> 00:05:45.789
The Cosmopolitan magazine made their first
cover from an image that was made by an AI.

00:05:45.789 --> 00:05:52.270
No tricks, no frills, just a good old image
straight out of DALL-E 2.

00:05:52.270 --> 00:05:57.099
And the kicker is that some of them are already
good enough to become magazine covers.

00:05:57.099 --> 00:05:59.810
That is incredible.

00:05:59.810 --> 00:06:02.879
Talk about the age of AI image creation!

00:06:02.879 --> 00:06:08.340
Four, this tool can even help us create new
product designs.

00:06:08.340 --> 00:06:14.000
And I mean not this one, although this toilet
car might have some utility if you need to

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:18.199
go when you are on the go, but I meant this
one instead!

00:06:18.199 --> 00:06:20.699
And, finally, five.

00:06:20.699 --> 00:06:28.639
We can also combine DALL-E 2 with other tools
that take a 2D image and try to build an understanding

00:06:28.639 --> 00:06:31.160
as if it were a 3D scene.

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:37.070
And the results are truly stunning, we can
get so much more out of these images.

00:06:37.070 --> 00:06:42.800
And one of the important lessons here is that
not only AI-generated art is improving at

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:48.670
an incredible pace, but an additional lesson
is that everything is connected.

00:06:48.670 --> 00:06:55.240
So many of these tools can be made even more
powerful if we use our imagination and combine

00:06:55.240 --> 00:06:57.180
them correctly.

00:06:57.180 --> 00:06:58.349
This is huge.

00:06:58.349 --> 00:07:06.400
For instance, NVIDIA is already building virtual
copies of the real world around us.

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:07.860
Why is that?

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:13.980
Well, because this way we can reenact real
situations for their self-driving cars, and

00:07:13.980 --> 00:07:20.979
even create arbitrarily complex new situations,
and these AIs will be able to learn from them

00:07:20.979 --> 00:07:22.270
in a safe environment.

00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:28.039
Also, self-driving can also be combined with
a number of other technologies that make it

00:07:28.039 --> 00:07:30.860
an even more amazing experience.

00:07:30.860 --> 00:07:32.460
See the assistant there?

00:07:32.460 --> 00:07:37.889
It sees and identifies the passenger, and
understands natural language.

00:07:37.889 --> 00:07:44.300
It also understands which building is which
and what shows are played in them today, so

00:07:44.300 --> 00:07:50.000
we might jump into the car not even knowing
where we wish to go, and it would not only

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:54.939
help us find a good show, but it would also
drive us there.

00:07:54.939 --> 00:07:56.669
And, +1.

00:07:56.669 --> 00:07:59.159
Remember the shoe design example?

00:07:59.159 --> 00:08:06.139
How about trying on pieces of clothing, but
not one by one, as we do in real life, but

00:08:06.139 --> 00:08:10.610
trying on…all of the clothes, at the same
time.

00:08:10.610 --> 00:08:17.419
Yes, these are all AI-generated images, and
it is not on just one still image, but video

00:08:17.419 --> 00:08:20.909
footage where a camera moves around.

00:08:20.909 --> 00:08:23.129
This is spectacular.

00:08:23.129 --> 00:08:28.009
Imagine what buying clothes will look like
when we have algorithms like this!

00:08:28.009 --> 00:08:29.009
Wow.

00:08:29.009 --> 00:08:34.580
Or, if an actor did not have the appropriate
attire for a scene in a movie?

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:38.380
Not to worry, just change it in post with
the AI.

00:08:38.380 --> 00:08:39.899
How cool is that?

00:08:39.899 --> 00:08:43.360
You see, once again, everything is connected.

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:46.490
So, does this get your mind going?

00:08:46.490 --> 00:08:50.010
What would you combine with DALL-E 2?

00:08:50.010 --> 00:09:42.800
Thanks for watching and for 
your generous support, and I'll see 

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:44.290
you next time!

